<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan increase rate on pound sterling certs.</title>
<headline>Pakistan increase rate on pound sterling certs.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Tuesday that it increased the interest rate on five-year maturity foreign currency bearer certificates in pound sterling. However, the rates for U.S. dollar, Deutsche mark and yen certificates would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>Rates effective January 1:</p>
<p> Currency	     January 1-31/97    December 1-31/96</p>
<p> U.S. dollar	  8.50		   8.50 percent per annum</p>
<p> Pound sterling     9.75		   9.50 percent per annum</p>
<p> Deutsche mark	7.00		   7.00 percent per annum</p>
<p> Japanese yen	 4.00		   4.00 percent per annum</p>
</text>
